cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SituCraft in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "SituCraft"
abstract: "A local-first workbench for imaging-based spatial transcriptomics, starting with 10x Genomics Xenium: bundle validation, a larger-than-memory tissue viewer, quality control, built-in transcript-informed cell segmentation and the comparison of segmentations, pathology registration and review, cell typing, spatial neighborhood analysis and cohort comparison, with every decision recorded. It runs locally as one self-contained program, needs no other software, and keeps the user's data on their computer."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: McDermott
    given-names: Robert
repository-code: "https://github.com/robert-mcdermott/situcraft"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.8.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - imaging-based spatial transcriptomics
  - Xenium
  - cell segmentation
  - spatial omics
  - tissue analysis
